# oracle: pair lj/long/coul/long long long 2.5 with kspace pppm/disp 1.0e-4 under fix npt iso (the box changes every step, so the kspace setup is redone each step), automatic Coulomb G-ewald and grid, dispersion G-ewald and mesh given by the user (native's automatic values 1.451546425444761 and 36 36 36, so the case runs inside the test budget; the dispersion automatic path is in w253pd_coul_auto and w253pd_buck), charges +-0.5 on 108 fcc atoms, run 0 then 20 steps
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 6.6e-14, atoms 2.6e-14.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units           lj
atom_style      charge
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            * 1.0
group           odd id 1:108:2
set             group odd type 2
set             type 1 charge 0.5
set             type 2 charge -0.5
displace_atoms  all random 0.05 0.05 0.05 4421 units box
velocity        all create 1.44 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/long/coul/long long long 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 0.5 1.1
kspace_style    pppm/disp 1.0e-4
kspace_modify   gewald/disp 1.451546425444761 mesh/disp 36 36 36
timestep        0.005
fix             1 all npt temp 1.44 1.44 0.5 iso 1.0 1.0 2.0
thermo_style    custom step temp pe evdwl elong ecoul press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz vol
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             0
run             20
